"""Stage 3 surfaces for A36: the census family (appended last, kernel-only) and the P0 sentence for the case.
usage: python3 surfaces36.py <worktree> <label> <number of named results>"""
import json, os, sys, importlib.util
S = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('c36', os.path.join(S, 'rec', 'controls.py')); C = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(C)
W, label, NTHM = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3]
cen_path = os.path.join(W, 'verification/lean-manuscript-census.json')
c = json.load(open(cen_path, encoding='utf-8'))
assert not any('DitaHierarchy' in f.get('modules', []) for f in c['families'])
NOTE = {
 'A36-HIERARCHY': "Track B act 36, a native round under AGENTS.md §A.39, executed under the frozen control plane programmes/oi-qm/track-b/act-36-dita-hierarchy/preregistration.md, blob e6c17bd04bf52c96657efc25b788107ed5af8543. Outcome: A36-HIERARCHY. At act 29's product configuration Diţă's construction over any factorization of the sixteen-point carrier — an outer flat unitary factor on the first index set, inner flat unitary factors on the second, unit twist phases, and any bijections of the product with the carrier for rows and for columns — is unitary, flat and realizable in the column form (a36_shared_hull_g) and in the row form (a36_shared_hull_gt), with the 2 × 8 and 8 × 2 column instances at the frozen index maps stated concretely (a36_control_hull28, a36_control_hull82); through the certified rational stratum point F₄(z) ⊗ F₄(w), z = (3+4i)/5, w = (5+12i)/13, runs the family SIG ∘ u^W, W the frozen exponent matrix, whose every member at a unit u is a 2 × 8 column Diţă matrix at the frozen index maps, realizable in the product normalized set (a36_shared_line); the named point at u₆₀ = (60+i)/(60−i) is realizable, in the product normalized set and off the product-embedded stratum, its same-row-block, same-column-in-block cross ratio at (0,0,1,0,1,0) being u₆₀/256 (a36_shared_point); the family at u = 1 is the stratum point, on the stratum (a36_control_stratum). The verdict a36_hierarchy; the corollary a36_c_exclusive excludes the other verdict. " + NTHM + " named results, each within propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound; zero definitions against a budget of zero. The round's exact-computation probe verification/lean/dita_hierarchy_probe.py, run by the probes job, replays by integer and Gaussian-rational arithmetic: the defect 49 at the stratum point and 37 at the named point and at the second point u₅ = (3+4i)/5 of the family; the exhaustive block-structure searches, which find no 4 × 4 and no 8 × 2 Diţă factorization of either orientation at either point and exactly one 2 × 8 factorization of each orientation, while finding the known factorizations of the stratum point; the 492 4 × 4 Diţă hulls through the stratum point spanning its 49-dimensional defect at first order; the stabilizer of order 1024 with its residual sectors 8 + 8 + 4 + 2 + 1, the two 8-dimensional sectors obstructed at seeded generic directions by an exact cokernel certificate that fails at their structured basis vectors, and the 4-, 2- and 1-dimensional sectors extended by explicit row-hull corrections. These are exact arithmetic replayed, not kernel-certified; by them the 4 × 4 Diţă hierarchy is locally insufficient at the certified stratum point, and the first escaping family belongs to the 2 × 8 construction. Whether every realizable class near the stratum lies in some Diţă hull of some factorization is open, recorded and not decided. Act 35's recorded verdict and open modulus stand as recorded, the latter answered for the 4 × 4 hulls only; the product normalized set and its isometries are not classified. P0 stays OPEN; no hull, family, factorization or isometry is adopted as a physical symmetry, principle or law. Non-sealing.",
 'A36-NOT-HIERARCHY': "Track B act 36, a native round under AGENTS.md §A.39, executed under the frozen control plane programmes/oi-qm/track-b/act-36-dita-hierarchy/preregistration.md, blob e6c17bd04bf52c96657efc25b788107ed5af8543. Outcome: A36-NOT-HIERARCHY. The Diţă-hierarchy package fails at a named part, exhibited in the kernel; the 2 × 8 and 8 × 2 instances and the stratum control hold. Non-sealing.",
}
c['families'].append({'name': "the Diţă factorization hierarchy at the product-embedded stratum — Diţă's construction over any factorization of the sixteen-point carrier realizable in both forms, its 2 × 8 and 8 × 2 instances, an exact 2 × 8 family through the certified rational stratum point, and a named point of it off the stratum (act 36, Track B)",
                      'modules': ['DitaHierarchy'], 'status': 'kernel-only', 'manuscript': [], 'note': NOTE[label]})
open(cen_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(json.dumps(c, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + '\n')
road_path = os.path.join(W, 'verification/ROADMAP.md')
road = open(road_path, encoding='utf-8').read()
new = C.expected_roadmap(road, label)
assert new is not None and new != road
open(road_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(new)
print('surfaces written for', label)
